# jarvisd environment — copy to /etc/jarvisd/jarvisd.env and fill in.
#
# This file holds secrets. install.sh creates it 0600 root:root; keep it that way.
# Nothing here has a working default on purpose: every value that could weaken the
# daemon is absent until you set it, and the daemon refuses rather than guesses.

# ---- required -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The static bearer for the JSON API and MCP. With this UNSET the daemon runs with
# auth OFF, which is only ever appropriate on a loopback bind you fully trust.
# Generate one: openssl rand -hex 32
JARVIS_BEARER=

# ---- bind -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Loopback by default. Put a reverse proxy in front before changing this; the
# daemon is not written to be the thing facing the internet.
JARVIS_HOST=127.0.0.1
JARVIS_PORT=8790

# ---- storage ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# audit.jsonl and runs/ are written alongside the database.
JARVIS_DB=/var/lib/jarvisd/jarvis.db
JARVIS_WORKSPACE=/var/lib/jarvisd/workspace

# ---- Slack ingress (optional; leave blank to keep it shut) ------------------------
# From the Slack app's Basic Information page, "Signing Secret". With this UNSET,
# POST /api/slack/events answers 503 and processes nothing — it is off, not open.
#
# Setup, once this is set and the daemon is reachable over HTTPS:
#   1. Slash Commands -> Create New Command
#        Command:      /jarvis
#        Request URL:  https://<your-host>/api/slack/events
#      Typing "/jarvis ship the release notes" opens a goal and replies inline.
#   2. Optional, for "@jarvis do the thing": Event Subscriptions -> enable,
#      Request URL the same, subscribe the bot to `app_mention`. Slack sends a
#      url_verification challenge; the daemon verifies its signature before echoing.
#
# No bot token is needed for either of those: a slash command's HTTP response is
# the reply Slack shows, and an event post only wants a 2xx. A token would only be
# needed to post unprompted INTO a channel, which this daemon does not do.
JARVIS_SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---- brain (optional) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a provider AND its key, jarvis.ask returns a structured
# "brain unavailable" error rather than pretending to answer.
# JARVIS_BRAIN=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- rate limits (optional; sane defaults in config.py) ---------------------------
# JARVIS_RATE_IP=
# JARVIS_RATE_KEY=
# JARVIS_RATE_AGENT=
